 <h1>Learn</h1>
 <p class="byline">Plain-English guides on lenses, coatings and eye health, written by the Manh Long Optical team, 147A Le Duan, Cua Nam, Hanoi.</p>
 
-<div class="listing"><h3 class="grouphead" id="lenses">Lenses</h3><article><p class="cat">LENSES</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/essilor-stellest-myopia-control.html">Essilor Stellest: Myopia Control Lenses for Children</a></h2><p>Stellest 1.59 Airwear for ages 6 to 18: 7,200,000d a pair, how H.A.L.T. works, what the 67% figure means, and when you don't need it yet.</p></article><article><p class="cat">LENSES</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/essilor-eyezen-computer-lenses.html">Essilor Eyezen: Lenses for Heavy Screen Use</a></h2><p>Essilor Eyezen single-vision lenses for people on screens all day: light near-vision support, blue-violet light filtering. Prices from 1,780,000d a pair.</p></article><article><p class="cat">LENSES</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/essilor-authentic-check.html">How to Spot a Genuine Essilor Lens</a></h2><p>Essilor is one of the most counterfeited lens brands, precisely because it's so well known. Five checks: packaging, hidden logo, warranty card, coating feel, authorised dealer.</p></article><article><p class="cat">LENSES</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/varilux-comfort-max.html">Varilux Comfort Max: All-Day Comfort Progressives</a></h2><p>Essilor's comfort-leaning progressive lens. The difference shows up in your neck, not on a vision chart.</p></article><article><p class="cat">LENSES</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/photochromic-vs-polarized-sunglasses.html">Photochromic vs Polarized Lenses: Which Should You Choose?</a></h2><p>Polarized is sunglasses-only at this shop, photochromic can carry a prescription. Real prices from 350,000d, compared in detail at Manh Long Optical.</p></article><article><p class="cat">LENSES</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/blue-light-vs-uv-protection.html">Blue-Light Filtering and UV Protection: What's the Difference</a></h2><p>These two are usually sold as one line item, but they block two different wavebands from two different sources. How to tell them apart, and which one you actually need.</p></article><article><p class="cat">LENSES</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/lens-coatings-explained.html">Anti-Reflective, Anti-Scratch, Hydrophobic: What Each Lens Coating Does</a></h2><p>A clear lens today is almost never just glass or plastic. What each coating actually does, and which ones are worth paying for.</p></article><article><p class="cat">LENSES</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/varilux-physio-extensee.html">Varilux Physio Extensee Review: Worth the Upgrade?</a></h2><p>Essilor's higher-tier progressive design, built around a wider near-vision zone. Where it actually helps, and where it doesn't.</p></article><article><p class="cat">LENSES</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/essilor-lenses.html">Essilor Lenses: Where Your Money Goes</a></h2><p>Varilux, Crizal, Eyezen, Transitions — Essilor splits its lineup by the problem each line solves, not by price tier. What does each one actually do?</p></article><article><p class="cat">LENSES</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/essilor-transitions-price.html">Essilor Transitions Lenses: How Much Do They Cost?</a></h2><p>A pair that's clear indoors and dark outdoors. What Gen S actually changed, and what to ask before buying.</p></article><article><p class="cat">LENSES</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/transitions-gen-s-advantages.html">What's Better About Essilor Transitions Gen S</a></h2><p>Speed, color range, protection, optics, durability — what the 2024 generation actually improved, and what that means on your own face.</p></article><article><p class="cat">LENSES</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/photochromic-progressive-lenses.html">Photochromic Progressive Lenses: Two Jobs in One Lens</a></h2><p>One lens for every distance that also darkens in the sun and clears back indoors. How Essilor Transitions and Zeiss PhotoFusion X compare, and what to check before buying.</p></article><article><p class="cat">LENSES</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/zeiss-lenses.html">Zeiss Progressive Lenses: Sharp Vision at Every Distance</a></h2><p>One lens for far, intermediate and near vision, with no visible dividing line and no switching glasses. What makes Zeiss progressives different, and which line to pick.</p></article><article><p class="cat">LENSES</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/zeiss-smartlife-individual.html">Zeiss SmartLife Individual: A Lens Made to Measure for You</a></h2><p>SmartLife Individual is Zeiss's most personalized lens line — built around your own face, frame and viewing habits, not an average number.</p></article><article><p class="cat">LENSES</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/zeiss-uvprotect.html">Zeiss UVProtect: Blocking UV Up to 400 nm on a Clear Lens</a></h2><p>The 20 nanometer gap most clear lenses leave open, and how Zeiss closes it.</p></article><article><p class="cat">LENSES</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/chemi-lenses.html">Chemi Lenses: Stock or Custom-Ground, A-ONE or A-PLUS</a></h2><p>Chemi lenses: stock lenses cut same-day, custom-ground lenses take 10-15 days and cost 2.6 to 6.7 times more. September 2026 prices, 147A Le Duan, 0777 986 999.</p></article><article><p class="cat">LENSES</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/tokai-lenses.html">Tokai Lenses: Index 1.70, 1.76 and the Lutina Lens's 400-420 nm Cut</a></h2><p>Tokai lenses in Hanoi: 1.60, Lutina 1.67, 1.70 and 1.76, from 1,200,000 to 9,300,000 VND per pair. Lutina cuts the 400-420 nm band per Tokai's own claim. 0777 986 999.</p></article><h3 class="grouphead" id="coatings">Lens Coatings</h3><article><p class="cat">COATINGS</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/crizal-easy-pro.html">Crizal Easy Pro: What It Adds Over a Basic Coating</a></h2><p>Crizal Easy Pro: a real step up from a basic coating, not the top-tier price.</p></article><article><p class="cat">COATINGS</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/crizal-natural-look.html">Crizal Natural Look: 360-Degree Anti-Glare Coating</a></h2><p>Crizal Natural Look cuts reflections from every angle, not just head-on. What that means for photos, night driving and everyday wear.</p></article><h3 class="grouphead" id="guide">Buying Guides</h3><article><p class="cat">GUIDE</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/how-to-read-your-prescription.html">How to Read a Glasses Prescription: SPH, CYL, AXIS, ADD, PD</a></h2><p>How to read a glasses prescription: what OD/OS, Sphere (SPH), Cylinder (CYL), Axis, ADD and PD mean, what plus and minus signs mean, with a worked example.</p></article><article><p class="cat">GUIDE</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/contacts-vs-glasses.html">Contact Lenses or Glasses: Which Should You Choose?</a></h2><p>Both correct the same prescription, but comfort, lifestyle and eye health tip the scale differently for each person.</p></article><article><p class="cat">GUIDE</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/how-to-choose-glasses-that-fit.html">How to Choose Glasses That Actually Fit</a></h2><p>How to pick a frame for your face shape, the right lens index for your prescription, and the order to do an eye test in. Full guide from Manh Long Optical.</p></article><h3 class="grouphead" id="eye-health">Eye Health</h3><article><p class="cat">EYE HEALTH</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/astigmatism-night-vision.html">Astigmatism and Night Glare: Why Lights Look Worse After Dark</a></h2><p>Halos and starbursts around headlights and streetlights are a familiar sign of uncorrected astigmatism. Why it happens, and how lenses fix it.</p></article><article><p class="cat">EYE HEALTH</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/when-do-you-need-glasses.html">How Nearsighted Do You Need to Be Before You Need Glasses?</a></h2><p>There's no single diopter cutoff. What actually decides it is whether blur is affecting your daily life, not a number on a prescription.</p></article><h3 class="grouphead" id="children">Children's Eyewear</h3><article><p class="cat">CHILDREN</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/choosing-glasses-for-nearsighted-children.html">Choosing Glasses for Nearsighted Children</a></h2><p>Signs of nearsightedness in children, how often to test their eyes, and choosing a frame that survives a hyperactive kid. Free eye tests for children.</p></article><h3 class="grouphead" id="style">Style &amp; Fit</h3><article><p class="cat">STYLE</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/choosing-frames-face-shape.html">Choosing Frames That Suit Your Face Shape</a></h2><p>The old rule still holds: a frame should offset your face, not repeat it. How to read your own face shape before you go try frames on.</p></article><h3 class="grouphead" id="care">Care &amp; Maintenance</h3><article><p class="cat">CARE</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/caring-for-your-glasses.html">How to Clean and Care for Your Glasses the Right Way</a></h2><p>Most scratches and loose hinges come from a few very small daily habits. Here's what to change.</p></article><h3 class="grouphead" id="data">Data &amp; Research</h3><article><p class="cat">DATA</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/myopia-statistics-vietnam-2026.html">Myopia and refractive error in Vietnam: what the studies say (2026)</a></h2><p>Sourced figures from WHO, IAPB, Ophthalmology, PLoS One and Vietnamese journals, nine studies side by side, and why their numbers disagree. Every figure links to its publisher.</p></article><h3 class="grouphead" id="trivia">Fun Facts</h3><article><p class="cat">TRIVIA</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/why-phones-use-zeiss-lenses.html">Why Do Phone Makers Use Zeiss Lenses?</a></h2><p>Zeiss shows up on camera bumps from Nokia to Vivo. What the badge actually means, and what it has in common with the lenses in your glasses.</p></article><h3 class="grouphead" id="about">About Manh Long Optical</h3><article><p class="cat">ABOUT</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/manh-long-optical-since-2000.html">Manh Long Optical: 25 Years of Frames, Wholesale and Retail, Lens Partner to Essilor, Zeiss, Nikon</a></h2><p>25 years supplying frames wholesale and retail, a partner of Essilor, Zeiss and Nikon lenses — contact lenses, progressives to single-vision, specialty lenses, and modern fitting equipment.</p></article><article><p class="cat">ABOUT</p><h2><a href="/en/learn/why-choose-manh-long-optical.html">Why Do Many Customers Choose Manh Long Optical?</a></h2><p>5 criteria for a trustworthy optical shop: eye testing, product range, price, aftercare, real reviews. How Manh Long Optical measures up, including what it hasn't solved yet.</p></article></div>
